SUMMARY:Deadline: The David Prize 2026/27: USD 200\,000 each\, no strings a
 ttached\, for five New Yorkers with ideas for a better New York City
DESCRIPTION:The David Prize gives five New Yorkers USD 200\,000 each\, no s
 trings attached\, to pursue an idea that would make New York City better. 
 It is not an arts prize: no field or sector is named\, and ideas are judge
 d on being urgent and additive to the city. Artists\, technologists\, orga
 nisers\, researchers and anyone else can enter\, provided the idea is root
 ed in New York.\n\nOrganisation: The David Prize (Walentas Family Foundati
 on)\nLocation: New York City\, USA. For individuals who live and work in o
 ne of the five boroughs.\nAward: USD 200\,000 each to five individuals\, u
 nrestricted\, with no metrics or reporting asked of winners. No applicatio
 n fee mentioned.\nDuration: Open call to 30 November 2026\; finalists and 
 in-person interviews in summer 2027\n\nMore: https://thedavidprize.org/ste
 ps/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://thedavidprize.org/steps/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&
 utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:New York City\, USA. For individuals who live and work in one of t
 he five boroughs.
